  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Blueberries are put to the test against insulin resistance, oxidation, and DNA damage.</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">A famous pair of Harvard studies involved so many people over such long a time that they’ve </span><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22357723/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">accumulated</span></a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> millions of person-years of data. As I discuss in my video <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-blueberries-for-a-diabetic-diet-and-dna-repair/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flashback Friday: Blueberries for a Diabetic Diet and DNA Repair</strong></a>,</span> <span data-contrast=\"auto\">the studies found the consumption of anthocyanin-rich foods, those containing brightly colored plant pigments and “particularly blueberries,” was associated with a lower risk of developing type 2 diabetes. Just two or three servings of blueberries a week has been associated with a 23 percent lower risk. In my Daily Dozen, I recommend at least one serving of berries every day—a half-cup of fresh or frozen berries or a quarter-cup of dried.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">What do berries have to do with diabetes? Well, type 2 diabetes is caused by insulin resistance, and interventional studies “clearly </span><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20089785/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">showed</span></a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> that dietary BBE [berries] ameliorates insulin resistance.” Sounds good, but that </span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">was</span><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> in diabetic mice.</span> <span data-contrast=\"auto\">What happens in people? As you can see in the graph below and at 1:05 in my </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/blueberries-for-a-diabetic-diet-and-dna-repair/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b><span data-contrast=\"none\">video</span></b></a><span data-contrast=\"auto\">, those </span><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24336456/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">consuming</span></a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> a lot of anthocyanin-rich foods like berries didn’t just have less inflammation,</span> <span data-contrast=\"auto\">but significantly lower insulin resistance as well. By how much? By as much as you would get </span><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11130623/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">walking</span></a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> an hour or so a day, seven days a week.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93090\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-05-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">H</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">ow many berries were they eating?</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">They were getting </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW139723557 BCX0\">35</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW139723557 BCX0\">m</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW139723557 BCX0\">illi</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW139723557 BCX0\">g</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW139723557 BCX0\">rams</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\"> of anthocyanins a day</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">, which</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">, as you can see below and at 1:28 in my </span></span><strong><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW139723557 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/blueberries-for-a-diabetic-diet-and-dna-repair/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">video</span></span></a></strong><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">,</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">would </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW139723557 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28483533/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">be</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\"> equivalent to</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\"> a cup of strawberries or cherries, a half</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">–</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">cup of raspberries, a quarter</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">–</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">cup of blackberries, or just a few spoon</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">s</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">ful of blueberries. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">T</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">hat was just a snapshot-in-time cross-sectional study</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">, though</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">. What we </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW139723557 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24336456/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">need</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\"> are interventional trials, where you give people blueberries in a double-blind, randomized, and placebo-controlled clinical trial to truly put them to the test</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">, and we got just that</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139723557 BCX0\">.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW139723557 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93092\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-28-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW162344579 BCX0\">In order to</span> </span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW162344579 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20724487/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">fake</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"> <span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW162344579 BCX0\">out</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">people with a placebo</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\"> the</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\"> researchers</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\"> used powdered blueberries equivalent </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">to</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\"> about two cups of fresh blueberries in a smoothie</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">As you can see in the graph below and at 2:09 in my </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW162344579 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/blueberries-for-a-diabetic-diet-and-dna-repair/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><strong>video</strong></span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">, t</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">he results </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW162344579 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20724487/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">demonstrated</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\"> a </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW162344579 BCX0\">significant improvement in insulin sensitivity.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW162344579 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93094\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-09-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">There are a lot of blueberries in t</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">wo cups</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">!</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">What benefits could be </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">expected</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">for a typical half-cup serving? </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">Another</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> study </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW266202416 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22935321/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW266202416 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">demonstrated</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> a significant reduction in postprandial oxidation</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">—that is</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">, </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW266202416 BCX0\">all </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW266202416 BCX0\">of</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">the free radicals created when you eat some sugary breakfast like corn flakes. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">The a</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">ntioxidant capacity of your bloodstream tak</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">es</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> a nosedive two hours afterwards</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> as your body tries to cope. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW266202416 BCX0\">But</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW266202416 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> eat it with a </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">half-cup</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> of blueberries</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> and you</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">r antioxidant levels</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> start out higher and stay higher after the meal. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">T</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">he</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> researchers</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> also tried adding </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">just </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">a quarter</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">–</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">cup of blueberries, but that was not enough</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">.</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">S</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">o, we should strive for a full serving.</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\"> You can see a graph depicting this below and at 2:29 in </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW266202416 BCX0\">my</span> </span><strong><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW266202416 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/blueberries-for-a-diabetic-diet-and-dna-repair/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW266202416 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">video</span></span></a></strong><span class=\"TextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW266202416 BCX0\">.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW266202416 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93096\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/2-29-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">The reason we care about free radicals is </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">because</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> they can damage our DNA. Can a single </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">portion</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> of blueberries really improve protection against DNA damage?</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">Y</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">es! </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">Researchers</span> </span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW247383536 BCX0\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23507228/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW247383536 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">drew</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> blood from people before and after they ate some frozen blueberries</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">, then</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> exposed their white blood cells to free radicals in the form of hydrogen peroxide</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">. They found that</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> blueberr</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">ies </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">significantly reduced the DNA damage done within a single hour after berry consumption. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">“</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">However, the protective effect was transient</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">”</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> and our DNA vulnerability returned within two hours</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">.</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">So</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">, we </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">should</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> eat super healthy foods like berries at every meal. In conclusion, one </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">serving</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> of blueberries can improve our cellular resistance to DNA damage, </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">“</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">thus supporting the importance of consuming </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">vegetable foods</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\"> regularly.</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW247383536 BCX0\">”</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW247383536 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p class=\"p3\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"apple-converted-space\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;21aca07e-3cdf-460a-8fa3-fb1ea206389d|72&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;apple-converted-space&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;apple-converted-space&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,469778324,&#34;Default Paragraph Font&#34;]}\">Berries pack such a nutritional punch that I recommend eating at least </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"apple-converted-space\">half</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"apple-converted-space\"> a </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"apple-converted-space\">cup a day in my </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW139748412 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW139748412 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">Daily Dozen</span></span><span class=\"TextRun SCXW139748412 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><spa